husthelper / stdchar
====================

This directory contains LGPL-3.0 licensed code, separate from the MIT-licensed
core of husthelper.

Origin
------
The CAPTCHA recognition algorithm (per-frame/per-channel Otsu binarization,
temporal averaging, 4-strip splitting and Hamming-distance template matching)
and the bundled digit templates `char_0.npy` ... `char_9.npy` are ported from:

  HUST-CAS-login-emulator
  https://github.com/xuxinhang/HUST-CAS-login-emulator
  License: GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0

Files in this directory are therefore distributed under LGPL-3.0-or-later.
See ./LICENSE for the full license text.

Isolation from the MIT core
---------------------------
The MIT-licensed core never imports this directory. It talks to it only as a
separate process over stdin/stdout (see ../src/stdchar-pipe.ts and ./cli.ts),
so the core remains MIT while this component stays LGPLv3.

If you modify files in this directory, the resulting LGPL-covered work must be
made available under the same license (or later).
